{"duration_api_ms":28119,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0b9769b9-783e-4e34-91c0-31874b86d5e8","total_cost_usd":2.5405268000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":304864,"cache_read_input_tokens":201094,"output_tokens":3069,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1138},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":304864,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":613,"cache_read_input_tokens":201094,"cache_creation_input_tokens":73399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":73399},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":3069,"cacheReadInputTokens":201094,"cacheCreationInputTokens":304864,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.5405268000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1138,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote `coder-1.json`. It has one row, for `egi-draft-a1v2`, and the chair is **rung 2: \"Forbid rules that require schools to tell parents.\"**\n\n- **Her act:** Blanca Rubio voted Aye on AB 1955 (2023-2024) on 2024-06-27. That vote was the Assembly's concurrence in Senate amendments, so it was on the text that became law. The tally was 61-16, which is about 21% No, so the vote is not near-unanimous. She has been in office since 2016, so the vote is in-term.\n- **What the bill says:** Section 220.5 says a district \"shall not enact or enforce any policy, rule, or administrative regulation that would require an employee or a contractor to disclose\" a pupil's gender identity without the pupil's consent. That matches the rung-2 clause.\n- **Why not rung 1:** The bill only bars rules that force disclosure. It does not require staff to keep the information from parents. Rungs 3–5 all require telling parents, so the bill rules them out too.\n- **Namesake:** The bill page's \"Coauthor: Senator Rubio\" is a different legislator. I did not treat it as her act.\n- **Single-subject reading:** The bill also has sections on support resources for families and on protecting staff from retaliation. I treated it as one subject (pupil rights) and coded the passages `chair-shaped`. If a reviewer reads it as multi-subject instead, the vote can show only her side, not the rung.\n- **Preemption:** The bill stops school districts from setting their own rule, which the codebook usually codes as `adjacent`. I coded it `on-question` because rung 2 is itself about forbidding such rules.\n\n`rests_on` lists both snapshots: the vote page and the bill text. There are no quotes, because neither source has her own words, and `needs_source` is empty.","ttft_ms":11735,"type":"result","duration_ms":30084,"uuid":"43c42886-c175-4e3b-9016-c1260d90e92f","ttft_stream_ms":1727,"time_to_request_ms":164,"first_content_frame_ms":1727,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
